# Atlas Control Author Entry

Design controls in this repo live exclusively in the Atlas MCP
server `user-atlas-design-controls`. The end-to-end authoring
workflow is encoded as Cursor Skills under `.cursor/skills/`.

This rule routes you into the right skill.

## Triggers

Pick the right skill based on the request:

| Request                                                | Skill                                |
|--------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| "Audit this code / PR for design controls"             | `atlas-codebase-audit`               |
| "Add / update / retire a UN, DI, DO, Risk, VT, VAL"    | `atlas-control-author`               |
| "Wire traceability" or "record a verification run"     | `atlas-control-author`               |
| "Map this DO to code" or "ground design outputs"       | `atlas-do-mapper`                    |
| "Rewrite for clinicians" or "check for scope drift"    | `atlas-language-and-scope-review`    |

## Default orchestration

For non-trivial requests, the default flow is:

1. `atlas-codebase-audit` produces the evidence map.
2. `atlas-control-author` runs the decision engine, search-before-create,
   atomic write plan, and audit report.
3. `atlas-do-mapper` grounds DOs in real code.
4. `atlas-language-and-scope-review` runs the wording gate.

## Hard constraints (inherited)

These rules still apply and are not duplicated here:

- `.cursor/rules/atlas-design-controls-first.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/atlas-design-controls-validation.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/atlas-vt-enforcement.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/atlas-do-implementation-mapping.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/health-literacy.mdc`

In short:

- Atlas MCP is the only store. No local `design-controls/` YAMLs.
- New artefacts use the 8-hex dcId format only.
- Class C is not permitted in this product without prior CSO and
  QA/RA escalation.
- Class B DIs MUST link to at least one Risk and at least one
  VT with a recorded `pass` run.
- VT and VAL runs MUST be recorded via
  `record_verification_run` / `record_validation_run`.

